<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  eno.vn imported PROPERTY-rental refresh (scripts/apartments-weekly.sh) — started DAILY at 06:00 since 2026-10-13
  (owner: every rental property, 7 days at most, refreshed every 3 days). The label and file keep their old
  "apartments-weekly" name so the installed agent is replaced in place. Each source inside runs only when its last
  SUCCESS is at least 66 h old (scripts/apartments-gate.sh), so a healthy source refreshes every 3 days and a failed
  one retries the next morning; the daily 7-day sweep (scripts/expire-rentals.ts in its sweep mode) runs at the end of
  EVERY run — and, so a refresh that outlasts a day cannot cost it, on its own agent too (vn.eno.rentals-sweep, 05:30,
  scripts/vn.eno.rentals-sweep.plist: install both).
  ⛔ APT_PLACES (EnvironmentVariables below) is the owner's call on photo storage: 0 = apartments only (the import scope
  of before 2026-10-13; the daily sweep still takes every type down past 7 days, so no imported house, room or office
  is listed), 1 = houses, rooms and offices too (≈2 GB of photos a day instead of ≈0.7 — the job's header has the
  numbers). Change it here and reload this agent. From 1 back to 0: the sweep holds the places units' last cohort back
  (an alert every morning) until a person releases it with expire-rentals.ts --sweep --allow-mass-expiry (the header).
  The vehicle job starts at 05:00; the two crawl different hosts.
  It runs from ~/eno-apartments-job, a CLEAN detached worktree at origin/main — fast-forward it
  (a detached checkout of origin/main, then prisma generate) after a change to any
  importer, as with ~/eno-vehicles-job.
  Install (or update — the schedule changed from weekly to daily, so the agent must be reloaded):
    mkdir -p ~/eno-import-journals/apartments   # launchd will not start a job whose log dir is missing
    launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/vn.eno.apartments-weekly.plist 2>/dev/null
    cp scripts/vn.eno.apartments-weekly.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/ && launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/vn.eno.apartments-weekly.plist
  Remove: launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/vn.eno.apartments-weekly.plist
  A LaunchAgent runs in the logged-in GUI session, which the Batdongsan step needs (a headed Chrome:
  Cloudflare refuses headless). caffeinate keeps the Mac from idle-sleeping for the whole run (a lid-close still
  sleeps it: every database step re-checks the supervised tunnel); a run missed while the Mac sleeps fires on wake.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>vn.eno.apartments-weekly</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/bin/caffeinate</string>
    <string>-i</string>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>/Users/mk1e3/eno-apartments-job/scripts/apartments-weekly.sh</string>
    <string>--apply</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer></dict>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict><key>ENO_REPO</key><string>/Users/mk1e3/eno-apartments-job</string><key>APT_ENV_FILE</key><string>/Users/mk1e3/eno.vn/.env</string><key>PATH</key><string>/usr/local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string><key>APT_PLACES</key><string>0</string></dict>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key><string>/Users/mk1e3/eno-apartments-job</string>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/mk1e3/eno-import-journals/apartments/weekly.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/mk1e3/eno-import-journals/apartments/weekly.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
